      "id": 1,
      "text": "St. Pauls grew around the Virginia and Carolina Southern Railway, which sparked the construction of three cotton mills and made the town a textile hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        17,
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.stpaulsnc.gov/communityinformation",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors William Davis, who donated land for the first Presbyterian church in 1799.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Pauls%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Gilmore‑Patterson Farm and Kenneth McKinnon House, listed on the National Register of Historic Places, showcase St. Pauls’ 18th‑century heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Pauls%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Three cotton mills once powered St. Pauls, but after most closed in the 1990s, the town attracted new corporate investments in the 2010s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        22,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Pauls%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "When St. Pauls’ schools integrated, the former high school for African Americans was repurposed as an elementary school.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Pauls%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
